  "body": "**What happens.** In a second setup that holds the part turned (part alignment, for example flipped 180° about X), 3D operations are refused. The message is: `setup 'Setup 2' holds the part turned (part alignment) - 3D Pocket is not supported yet in an aligned setup (Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive are)`. A flipped setup also refuses picks and area controls.\n\n**Where the user hits it.** A 30 mm cube with R3.125 mm fillets on every edge, machined from two sides. Setup 1 can finish the top fillets. The bottom fillets and the bottom-notch floor fillets need 3D work in the flipped Setup 2, so today they stay unmachined (2D only).\n\n**Expected.** 3D Pocket and 3D Finish (and 3D Adaptive) generate in a flipped setup: in the setup's own frame, judged against the part as that setup holds it, with the same gouge laws as an unturned setup. A pose that the generator cannot handle is refused by name.\n\n**Related.** #763 (one machining-frame seam: OpFrame composes part_alignment and TiltedFrame) is the groundwork. #874 is the side-on (90°) case.\n\n**Done means:** a 3D Pocket and a 3D Finish on a part flipped 180° about X generate, verify and post. The pins show no gouge on the flipped part, and the path is identical to the same op on the unflipped part, mapped through the flip.\n",
